        "content": "type: event_result\nid: evt-7aBCD48CXL2HGDj\nprovider: luma\ntitle: Build your first app with AI in one evening\ndescription: \"A hands-on AI workshop for any professional. Whether you use ChatGPT every day or you secretly suspect you've fallen behind.\\n(This is already our 7th workshop — all sold out, so be fast. Our groups are intentionally small, and we do care about quality!)\\nMost people are still using AI through a chat box and in native apps. Coding agents work differently. You give them a task and they go execute it. Faster, more powerful, and almost nobody outside engineering teams has tried them yet.\\nOne workshop with us is enough to flip the switch. You'll set up Claude Code, Codex, or Gemini CLI on your laptop, build a working app with us, and walk out knowing how to build whatever you want next.\\nUnderstanding the concept will enable you to easily switch between different providers when the time comes. And the times of paying a middleman are clearly over.\\nApps are the easiest way to see how it works, but the same coding agent will help you research a topic in depth, wrangle a messy spreadsheet, draft and edit documents, or automate the small repetitive tasks that eat your week.\\nWe will also do a follow-up online call (2h - the exact date will be communicated).\\nYou'll walk away with\\nA working to-do app you built yourself, running on your own laptop. Simple by design: small enough to finish in one morning, concrete enough to show you the whole concept. By the end you'll understand how a coding agent reads your prompts, writes code, and turns it into something running on your machine.\\nAn AI coding agent (Claude Code, Codex, or Gemini CLI) set up on your laptop, and the confidence to actually use it. You'll know how to start a fresh project from a blank folder, write prompts the agent can act on, get unstuck when things go wrong, and turn the result into something usable.\\nA starter pack of recipes for the projects people actually build after this workshop: a daily journal, an inbox triage helper, a small website, or a simple mobile productivity app. Copy them, adapt them, ship them.\\nTh\"\nurl: \"https://lu.ma/30jul-first-app\"\ndate_start: \"2026-07-30T16:00:00.000Z\"\ndate_end: \"2026-07-30T19:00:00.000Z\"\ntimezone: Europe/Berlin\nevent_type: PHYSICAL\nvenue_name: null\nvenue_full_address: null\nvenue_short_address: null\nvenue_city: Berlin\nvenue_state: Berlin\nvenue_country: Germany\nvenue_country_code: DE\nvenue_lat: 52.48007770552034\nvenue_lon: 13.442950493962611\norganizer_name: Handpicked Berlin\norganizer_avatar_url: \"https://images.lumacdn.com/calendars/q8/c97b8a3b-9ca4-46ec-86d4-00fe45067ef2\"\norganizer_slug: handpicked\nhosts[2]{name,avatar_url}:\n  Igor Ranc,\"https://images.lumacdn.com/avatars/f0/ea3d68dd-d2bb-441e-8236-3067558c04ae.jpg\"\n  Phil Bennett,\"https://images.lumacdn.com/avatars/0m/7a0af3f5-6c12-4864-8379-3a8013a3c7ab.jpg\"\nrsvp_count: null\nis_paid: false\ncover_url: \"https://images.lumacdn.com/uploads/wl/3dcaf15d-1f81-43a8-8edf-37c62e9fe885.png\"\ncity: Berlin\ncountry: Germany\nimage_url: \"https://images.lumacdn.com/uploads/wl/3dcaf15d-1f81-43a8-8edf-37c62e9fe885.png\"\nhash: f6483f9fee95f2e4\nembed_ref: build-your-first-K18\napp_id: events\nskill_id: search",
